These FLAC files (and their .m4a, .mka, .mkv and .mp4 remuxes) are part of this repository and under its MIT licence (see LICENSE at the root).

The audio is synthetic: it is generated by the tests' own integer-only signal code in src/flac/tests.rs, so it is the same on every platform, and no recorded audio is in them. Each file was encoded once from that PCM with the reference FLAC encoder (flac 1.5.0, --no-padding, with the block size, order and stereo options its name gives) and remuxed with ffmpeg's -c:a copy. expected.txt holds the 64-bit hash of each file's decoded PCM.
